## std.fs — file system read.
##
## From docs/spec.md §6.4 (System Surfaces): read_file is exposed as
## a free-fn form after the user writes `pub import std.fs.{read_file}`.
## The router entry in src/codegen/builtins.zig maps `read_file`
## (arity=1) to the `fs_read_file` dispatch.
##
## Phase 2 real emit (merged from the prior `@panic` runtime stub):
## zig 0.16 retired `vendor/zig/lib/std/fs.zig` to a 21-line
## deprecation-stub file. The canonical read-file entry moved to
## `std.Io.Dir.readFileAlloc(dir, io, sub_path, gpa, limit)`, which
## requires a `std.Io` event-loop instance.
##
## The codegen-router emit (see src/codegen/expr.zig's
## `.fs_read_file` arm) per-call wraps the readFileAlloc invocation
## in a blk that owns the Io context:
##   `var __io_threaded = std.Io.Threaded.init(std.heap.page_allocator, .{});`
##   `defer __io_threaded.deinit();`
## so each `read_file(path)` call gets a fresh Threaded Io on its
## stack, tearable down via `defer` at the blk scope's exit
## (post-`break :blk` capture).
##
## Memory model (Phase 2 surface, conservative):
##   - Allocator: `std.heap.page_allocator`. Each successful read
##     allocates a fresh heap byte-slice for the file contents.
##   - Ownership: caller OWNS the returned `[]u8`. User MUST free
##     via `std.heap.page_allocator.free(slice)` before discarding;
##     page-aligned leaks at process exit are tolerable for short-
##     lived binaries (a v1 limitation).
##   - Phase 2.1 widening (deferred) will add a `free <slice>` overload
##     to `.free_expr` so the .zag surface gets a cleaner
##     `defer free data` syntax.
##
## Error model: `catch &[_]u8{}` silently coalesces every error
## (the `Io.Dir.Reader.Error || std.mem.Allocator.Error ||
## Io.UnexpectedError` triple-union) into an empty slice. v1 docs/18
## error-propagation contract isn't wired here yet — Phase 3 may
## add a sibling `read_file_or` builtin that bubbles specific errors
## via zag's `?` operator.
##
## Stub: throwaway body for the existing .zag parse-stubs-out
## convention. The (now-real) router arm REWRITES the call site
## before any reader sees the verbatim form, so the body never
## executes at runtime.

pub fun read_file(path: str) -> []u8 {
    return &[_]u8{};
}
